From: KB2UKA <kb2uka80@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dts): j713: attach NVMe storage system power domain

Attach J713 NVMe to APCIE_SYS_ST rather than its parent APCIE_ST.
APCIE_SYS_ST already depends on ANS and APCIE_ST, so the full storage
system domain participates in the consumer's runtime power reference.
Keep the override at board level; only J713 has been tested.

In bounded native Linux RAM boots with identical kernel, initramfs and
boot arguments, the old attachment reports an RTKit firmware SError
before controller initialization. Changing only this phandle allows
controller initialization and partition discovery. A follow-up direct
read probe reads the first MiB twice with matching hashes while the
block device is read-only. No filesystem is mounted or installed.
The boots used reduced-device bench DTs. The full-board DTB from this
patch was compiled and compared, but has not been booted.
The exact faulty firmware access is not established by these results.

Credit: KB2UKA
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
@@ -82,3 +82,4 @@
 &nvme {
+	power-domains = <&ps_ans>, <&ps_apcie_sys_st>;
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "okay";
 };
